claimed: okay-script-cluster-sessions -- operator ask 2026-09-06: clustered sessions over okay-persist's replicated store. Sessions.shared(topic: Topic, ttl, pollMs): the persisted engine over ANY Topic -- a Replicated coordinator on the leader node, a RemoteStore topic over the wire on the others -- with the in-memory index kept current by TAILING the topic (a consumer that applies what it reads; last write in log order wins), so a cart set on node A is read on node B. Sessions gains close() to stop the tailer. Tests: two Sessions.shared over one Replicated topic in-process; the same over Wire.Server + RemoteStore on a real port (Live). Touches Sessions.scala, specs/okay-script.md; no build.sbt change (okayPersist.jvm already a main dependency).
